# Notes on Wazuh configurations
At the moment I haven't set up SSL for HTTPS connections to my server, and setting up Nginx to use a mix of HTTP and HTTPS for Wazuh was being somewhat problematic, so I instead decided to reconfigure it to not use SSL. With the following changes I managed to get it working with the reverse proxy:

## Dashboard Configuration
File: `/etc/wazuh-dashboard/opensearch_dashboards.yml`

Commented out:
~~~
#server.ssl.enabled: true
#server.ssl.key: "/usr/share/wazuh-dashboard/certs/wazuh-dashboard-key.pem"
#server.ssl.certificate: "/usr/share/wazuh-dashboard/certs/wazuh-dashboard.pem"
# opensearch_security.cookie.secure: true
~~~
Changes server.host to 127.0.0.1 and server.port to 5601

## API Configuration
File: `/var/ossec/api/configuration/api.yaml`

Uncommented and changed the following lines:
~~~
host: ['127.0.0.1', '::1']
port: 55000
https:
  enabled: false
~~~

## Wazuh General Config
File: `/usr/share/wazuh-dashboard/data/wazuh/config/wazuh.yml`

Changed the URL of the host at the bottom of the file to http (from https).

## Future
When I implement SSL in my server I will revert some configurations to use HTTPS again
